<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Székelys</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Szeklers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Székelys, or Szeklers, are a Hungarian-speaking people living mainly in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>. In the medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a> they served as frontier guards and light cavalry and held collective liberties as one of the three privileged 'nations' of Transylvania, alongside the nobility and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a>. Their origins are debated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/szekelys.jpg" alt="Székelys" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Székelyzászló(SZNT).png: unknown derivative work: Qorilla · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Szekely_Land.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
